<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Otago</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Otago is a region in the south-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a>'s South Island, with Dunedin as its main city. It was settled from 1848 by a Free <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/church-of-scotland">Church of Scotland</a> colony, and the discovery of gold at Gabriel's Gully in 1861 set off the Otago gold rush, which for a time made Dunedin the largest town in New Zealand. Its economy later rested on sheep farming, and it is home to the University of Otago, founded in 1869.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/otago.jpg" alt="Otago" width="320" height="404" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Peetel Derived from File:New Zealand location map.svg · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Otago_Region_location_in_New_Zealand.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In the Archaic or “moa-hunter” period, from settlement to about 1500, most villages lay on or near the coast, the <b>Otago</b> region was the centre of cultural development, and people set up temporary inland camps to hunt.</blockquote><a href="/culture/maori">Māori · Society</a></li><li><blockquote>It was won by John Joseph Woods of Lawrence, <b>Otago</b>, born in Van Diemen's Land, who wrote the melody in a single sitting on the evening after he heard of the competition.</blockquote><a href="/songs/god-defend-new-zealand">God Defend New Zealand</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1831 they founded a whaling station at <b>Otago</b> Heads, near present-day Dunedin in the South Island, seventeen years before Dunedin was established, and from 1833 they sold provisions to whalers from their base at Otakou, which they named &quot;Otago&quot;.</blockquote><a href="/songs/wellerman">Soon May the Wellerman Come</a></li><li><blockquote>Wool, gold from <b>Otago</b> and, after 1882, refrigerated meat drove the economy.</blockquote><a href="/state/colony-of-new-zealand">Colony of New Zealand</a></li></ul></section>
